# Line endings are part of this repo's CORRECTNESS, not just tidiness.
#
# Several suites are SOURCE-CONTRACT tests: they read a source file as a string and assert it contains an
# exact multi-line snippet, or hash its bytes. Those comparisons are line-ending sensitive. Without this
# file, a checkout inherits the machine's `core.autocrlf` — Git for Windows defaults it to `true` — so a
# fresh clone lands CRLF and three suites fail with mismatched hashes and "expected ... to contain ...".
#
# Proven, not assumed: a clean clone of this branch on a machine with the default setting failed
#   - flourish raw Arena cancellation panel (multi-line snippet match)
#   - B56 belt-mode permanent regressions (indexOf returned -1)
#   - B24 shared radial fallback removal (content hash mismatch)
# while the same commit passed 3011/3011 in an LF working copy.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` normalizes on checkout everywhere, so every machine — and CI — sees the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched. `text=auto` detects most of these, but the game's art and audio are
# the last thing that should depend on heuristics.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.wav binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.pdf binary

# Windows-only scripts genuinely need CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
